h. right to obtain facilitation in the judicial process; and/or
i. right to assistance.
(2) Children who become victims of violence, in addition to obtaining the rights as referred to in paragraph (1), also obtain special rights, as follows:
a. right to respect for survival, growth and development;
b. right to basic services;
c. right to receive spiritual guidance;
d. right to equal protection;
e. right to be free from various stigma; and/or
f. right to obtain freedom.

Article 13
Every person who knows, sees, or hears the occurrence of domestic violence is obligated to make efforts according to their capacity to:
a. prevent the continuation of the criminal act;
b. provide protection to the victim;
c. provide emergency assistance; and/or
d. assist in the process of submitting a request for a protection order.

Article 14
(1) Prevention as intended in Article 14 paragraph (1):
a. family and/or closest relatives;
b. Non-Governmental Organizations.

